WEBVTT

00:00:02.730 --> 00:00:04.770
<i>Wealth, fame, power...</i>

00:00:04.770 --> 00:00:06.670
<i>Gold Roger,
the King of the Pirates,</i>

00:00:06.670 --> 00:00:08.970
<i>attained everything
this world has to offer.</i>

00:00:08.970 --> 00:00:12.840
<i>The words he uttered just before
his death drove people to the seas.</i>

00:00:12.840 --> 00:00:16.680
<i>My treasure? If you want it,
you can have it!</i>

00:00:16.680 --> 00:00:20.240
<i>Find it! I left everything
this world has to offer there!</i>

00:00:22.850 --> 00:00:27.590
<i>And so men head for the Grand Line
in pursuit of their dreams!</i>

00:00:27.590 --> 00:00:31.490
<i>The world has truly entered
a Great Pirate Era!</i>

00:00:31.490 --> 00:00:36.860
<i>We're going to gather up
all our dreams</i>

00:00:36.860 --> 00:00:42.770
<i>and set out in search
of something to find</i>

00:00:42.770 --> 00:00:44.100
<i>ONE PIECE!</i>

00:00:49.040 --> 00:00:54.620
<i>Compasses only cause delays</i>

00:00:54.620 --> 00:01:00.350
<i>Delirious with fever,
I take the helm</i>

00:01:00.350 --> 00:01:10.350
<i>If the dusty treasure map has
been verified, it's not a legend!</i>

00:01:12.470 --> 00:01:18.170
<i>When it comes to personal storms,</i>

00:01:18.170 --> 00:01:23.480
<i>simply ride aboard
someone else's biorhythm</i>

00:01:23.480 --> 00:01:27.150
<i>and pretend it isn't there!</i>

00:01:27.150 --> 00:01:32.650
<i>We're going to gather up
all our dreams</i>

00:01:32.650 --> 00:01:38.360
<i>and set out in search
of something to find</i>

00:01:38.360 --> 00:01:44.600
<i>A coin in my pocket,
and do you wanna be my friend?</i>

00:01:44.600 --> 00:01:49.970
<i>We are, We are on the cruise!</i>

00:01:49.970 --> 00:01:51.040
<i>We are!</i>

00:02:22.440 --> 00:02:26.440
Terrible news, everyone!

00:02:26.440 --> 00:02:29.410
Pirates are attacking!

00:02:29.410 --> 00:02:31.650
Pirates! Pirates!

00:02:31.650 --> 00:02:34.420
Pirates are attacking!

00:02:34.420 --> 00:02:37.350
Run for your lives!

00:02:37.350 --> 00:02:43.020
Pirates! Run for your lives!

00:02:43.020 --> 00:02:51.690
"Liar of Justice?
Captain Usopp"

00:02:59.040 --> 00:03:02.980
It'd be reckless to go straight
into the Grand Line now!

00:03:05.950 --> 00:03:08.850
<i>Yeah, some meat would
be nice to have first.</i>

00:03:09.850 --> 00:03:12.590
Eating nothing but fruit everyday
is no good...

00:03:12.590 --> 00:03:14.660
Need some booze, too!

00:03:14.660 --> 00:03:16.820
What're you talking about?!

00:03:18.490 --> 00:03:19.860
That's not what I mean!

00:03:19.860 --> 00:03:23.900
The Grand Line is the most
dangerous place in the world!

00:03:23.900 --> 00:03:27.940
On top of that, it's crawling with
strong pirates after the One Piece!

00:03:27.940 --> 00:03:30.340
And they're all on powerful ships,
of course!

00:03:30.340 --> 00:03:32.540
We need more people, too.

00:03:32.540 --> 00:03:36.410
The number of crew members,
the lack of equipment on this ship...

00:03:36.410 --> 00:03:39.310
There's no way we could
survive like this!

00:03:39.310 --> 00:03:42.680
Yeah, we need a cook.
And a musician.

00:03:42.680 --> 00:03:44.020
A musician?!

00:03:45.590 --> 00:03:47.320
You're so stupid...

00:03:48.690 --> 00:03:53.030
A little to the south of here is
an island with people living on it.

00:03:53.030 --> 00:03:57.930
It'd be best if we can get
ahold of a real ship there...

00:03:57.930 --> 00:04:00.100
Alright! Time to eat some meat!

00:04:00.100 --> 00:04:01.740
Don't forget the booze!

00:04:01.740 --> 00:04:03.730
You guys!

00:04:08.510 --> 00:04:13.210
Pirates are here! Pirates!

00:04:14.220 --> 00:04:19.210
Everyone run away!
Pirates are here!

00:04:20.550 --> 00:04:23.420
Pirates!

00:04:23.420 --> 00:04:25.420
Terrible news!

00:04:28.200 --> 00:04:30.190
Pi... rates...

00:04:35.070 --> 00:04:37.770
The pirates...

00:04:37.770 --> 00:04:39.760
...are just a lie!

00:04:43.840 --> 00:04:45.750
Oww...

00:04:46.750 --> 00:04:50.320
You exaggeration-spewing kid!
I'm gonna get you today for sure!

00:04:50.320 --> 00:04:52.320
Stay right where you are!

00:04:52.320 --> 00:04:54.310
I'll show you a thing or two!

00:04:57.090 --> 00:05:00.460
Here they come!
Here they come! Here they come!

00:05:00.460 --> 00:05:02.490
Get back here, you damn kid!

00:05:04.270 --> 00:05:07.600
Just try and catch me!

00:05:07.600 --> 00:05:10.040
Come and get me!

00:05:14.980 --> 00:05:18.410
Dammit! He got away again!

00:05:18.410 --> 00:05:23.250
--He's one hell of a troublemaker!
--He's in trouble if I find him!

00:05:23.250 --> 00:05:25.450
Where the hell'd he go?!

00:05:35.600 --> 00:05:37.630
Another job well done today!

00:05:37.630 --> 00:05:41.660
I sent the wind of excitement
into this boring village!

00:05:43.300 --> 00:05:45.740
There he is!

00:05:45.740 --> 00:05:47.610
Oh, it's you guys!

00:05:47.610 --> 00:05:50.280
Good morning, Captain Usopp!

00:05:50.280 --> 00:05:53.270
The Usopp Pirates have arrived!

00:05:55.450 --> 00:05:56.850
Pepper! Carrot!

00:05:56.850 --> 00:05:59.510
Is it just you two?
Where's Onion?

00:06:02.860 --> 00:06:06.560
Terrible news! Terrible news!

00:06:06.560 --> 00:06:08.660
Oww!

00:06:08.660 --> 00:06:10.630
Terrible news!

00:06:10.630 --> 00:06:13.630
--Onion...
--What's he freaking out about?

00:06:13.630 --> 00:06:16.000
Terrible news! Terrible news!

00:06:16.000 --> 00:06:19.040
Terrible news! Pirates are here!

00:06:19.040 --> 00:06:22.480
There's a boat with a skull mark
at the north shore!

00:06:22.480 --> 00:06:23.810
Yeah, right!

00:06:25.810 --> 00:06:27.720
It's the truth!

00:06:27.720 --> 00:06:30.080
T-the truth?

00:06:30.080 --> 00:06:33.020
It's true! This is bad!

00:06:33.020 --> 00:06:36.260
Oops! It's time for my snack!

00:06:36.260 --> 00:06:38.530
Don't run away!

00:06:38.530 --> 00:06:44.570
Actually, I have "I'll Die if
I Don't Eat My Snacks-iosis"!

00:06:44.570 --> 00:06:46.770
Liar!

00:06:46.770 --> 00:06:51.110
Don't you want to be
a real pirate, Captain?!

00:06:51.110 --> 00:06:54.740
What good is a pirate
who's afraid of pirates?!

00:06:54.740 --> 00:06:58.050
If I recall correctly,
it was Buggy the Clown's mark!

00:06:58.050 --> 00:07:01.710
B- B- Buggy the Clown?!

00:07:03.680 --> 00:07:06.250
I think I'll just...

00:07:06.250 --> 00:07:09.620
But it was two small boats!

00:07:09.620 --> 00:07:12.730
And three people or so...

00:07:12.730 --> 00:07:15.630
Alright! Let's go,
Usopp Pirates!

00:07:15.630 --> 00:07:18.300
To protect this
village's peace!

00:07:18.300 --> 00:07:20.700
Alright, let's go!
Follow me!

00:07:21.700 --> 00:07:23.030
R-right!

00:07:32.750 --> 00:07:36.920
Finally on dry land again...

00:07:36.920 --> 00:07:38.590
There's a village past here?!

00:07:38.590 --> 00:07:41.760
Yeah. It looks like
it's a small one, though...

00:07:41.760 --> 00:07:42.760
Oh!

00:07:42.760 --> 00:07:45.290
In that case, meat, meat!
Meat, meat, meat!

00:07:45.290 --> 00:07:47.160
There's a place to eat
in this village, right?!

00:07:47.160 --> 00:07:49.490
Forget about meat for a minute,
will you?!

00:07:54.600 --> 00:07:55.930
Huh?!

00:07:58.740 --> 00:08:00.670
Careful!

00:08:00.670 --> 00:08:02.240
I sense people!

00:08:02.240 --> 00:08:04.610
Where?! Where?! Where?!

00:08:04.610 --> 00:08:05.940
Look out!

00:08:21.400 --> 00:08:23.060
So cool!

00:08:23.060 --> 00:08:24.930
Is this the time
to be impressed?!

00:08:27.600 --> 00:08:31.940
I am Usopp, leader of the great
pirates who reign over this village!

00:08:31.940 --> 00:08:37.710
People praise me - and then praise
me more - as "Captain Usopp"!

00:08:38.880 --> 00:08:39.980
Huh?

00:08:39.980 --> 00:08:43.750
If you're thinking of attacking
this village, then forget it!

00:08:43.750 --> 00:08:48.760
My 80 million subordinates
won't sit by quietly!

00:08:48.760 --> 00:08:53.130
Awesome!

00:08:54.500 --> 00:08:56.200
You're lying, aren't you?

00:08:56.200 --> 00:08:58.430
Yikes! She saw through it!

00:08:58.430 --> 00:09:00.830
See, you admitted it.

00:09:02.200 --> 00:09:05.800
I admitted it to her!

00:09:08.340 --> 00:09:10.380
What?! He was lying?!

00:09:10.380 --> 00:09:12.450
Curse you, you crafty tactician!

00:09:12.450 --> 00:09:14.580
80 million may have
been an exaggeration,

00:09:14.580 --> 00:09:16.980
but I do have great men
under my command!

00:09:23.590 --> 00:09:25.750
<i>Like maybe three people?</i>

00:09:27.390 --> 00:09:29.600
She saw through it!

00:09:29.600 --> 00:09:32.670
R-run!

00:09:32.670 --> 00:09:36.000
H-hey, you guys!
Don't run away!

00:09:37.470 --> 00:09:41.810
<i>I've never heard of pirates
using slingshots before!</i>

00:09:44.850 --> 00:09:47.180
You're neat!

00:09:48.180 --> 00:09:50.820
Hey, you!
Don't insult me!

00:09:50.820 --> 00:09:54.320
I'm a very proud man!

00:09:54.320 --> 00:09:58.130
Because of my great pride,
people call me,

00:09:58.130 --> 00:10:01.100
"Proud Usopp"!

00:10:02.260 --> 00:10:04.490
You saw it yourself just now!

00:10:05.500 --> 00:10:12.010
My slingshot skills are far greater
than your average pistol!

00:10:12.010 --> 00:10:16.410
Now that you've drawn your pistol,
put your life on the line.

00:10:16.410 --> 00:10:17.740
Huh?!

00:10:19.750 --> 00:10:22.910
I'm saying those aren't
for threatening people.

00:10:30.190 --> 00:10:34.320
<i>What you're looking at now
are real pirates!</i>

00:11:38.530 --> 00:11:43.230
Now that you've drawn your pistol,
put your life on the line.

00:11:43.230 --> 00:11:45.300
Huh?!

00:11:45.300 --> 00:11:49.290
I'm saying those aren't
for threatening people.

00:12:14.530 --> 00:12:20.170
R-real pirates definitely have way
more punch behind their words...

00:12:20.170 --> 00:12:21.660
Awesome...

00:12:30.140 --> 00:12:32.680
--We stole those lines!
--Eh?

00:12:32.680 --> 00:12:36.680
From Shanks,
a pirate I respect!

00:12:36.680 --> 00:12:38.850
S- Shanks?!

00:12:38.850 --> 00:12:43.290
You know Red-Haired Shanks,
the great pirate?!

00:12:43.290 --> 00:12:47.690
Yeah. Your dad's Yasopp, right?

00:12:47.690 --> 00:12:49.690
Eh?

00:12:58.710 --> 00:13:03.370
<i>Yeah, Yasopp is my old man...</i>

00:13:05.310 --> 00:13:08.280
<i>But how do you know that?</i>

00:13:08.280 --> 00:13:12.220
"Food"

00:13:17.520 --> 00:13:19.250
Good, huh?!

00:13:20.430 --> 00:13:23.130
I met him when I was a kid!

00:13:23.130 --> 00:13:25.500
So my old man's on Shanks' ship?

00:13:25.500 --> 00:13:27.830
Yep! You guys look the same,

00:13:27.830 --> 00:13:30.670
so when I first saw you,
I wondered...

00:13:30.670 --> 00:13:32.370
Really?!

00:13:32.370 --> 00:13:35.940
My old man's on such
an awesome ship?!

00:13:35.940 --> 00:13:40.210
I dunno about now,
but I bet he's still with him.

00:13:40.210 --> 00:13:44.210
<i>After all, your dad was
a good sharpshooter!</i>

00:14:01.030 --> 00:14:02.940
Awesome!

00:14:02.940 --> 00:14:07.070
That's nothing. I could even shoot
an ant right between the eyes!

00:14:11.710 --> 00:14:13.480
Y'know, Luffy,

00:14:13.480 --> 00:14:17.320
I got a kid named Usopp,
just about your age!

00:14:17.320 --> 00:14:19.820
You've already told me lots of times!
I'm sick of it!

00:14:19.820 --> 00:14:21.150
What?!

00:14:23.060 --> 00:14:26.830
Well, I'm gonna keep on
tellin' you more about him!

00:14:26.830 --> 00:14:30.630
It was sad to say goodbye,
but there was no other choice!

00:14:30.630 --> 00:14:35.800
There was but one reason:
the pirate flag was calling me!

00:14:39.970 --> 00:14:44.240
Stuck! Stuck!

00:14:46.080 --> 00:14:50.980
Usopp. I heard enough about you
to make my ears sore.

00:14:50.980 --> 00:14:53.420
Yasopp was a great pirate!

00:14:53.420 --> 00:14:55.560
Yeah, huh?!

00:14:55.560 --> 00:15:01.260
I'm proud of my old man, who leapt
onto these possibly-endless seas...

00:15:01.260 --> 00:15:03.900
...to live with his life
on the line!

00:15:03.900 --> 00:15:06.570
Then that makes this easier!

00:15:06.570 --> 00:15:09.740
Do you have any friends in this
village who know how to sail...

00:15:09.740 --> 00:15:13.040
...and anyone who can
supply a big ship?!

00:15:13.040 --> 00:15:15.940
As you can see,
it's just a tiny village...

00:15:15.940 --> 00:15:19.080
Sorry, but we can't
live up to your hopes.

00:15:19.080 --> 00:15:20.980
On the top of the hill...

00:15:20.980 --> 00:15:23.420
There was a huge mansion.

00:15:23.420 --> 00:15:25.650
Say! Do you know them, Usopp?!

00:15:25.650 --> 00:15:28.820
Think you could ask them
to help pay for one?

00:15:28.820 --> 00:15:30.020
You can't go there!

00:15:32.260 --> 00:15:36.260
I- I just remembered
something I hafta do!

00:15:36.260 --> 00:15:38.770
I have lots of influence here!

00:15:38.770 --> 00:15:41.170
Eat and drink as much
as you want!

00:15:41.170 --> 00:15:43.830
Alright! Later!

00:15:45.910 --> 00:15:48.810
Why was he in such a rush?

00:16:15.240 --> 00:16:17.360
You wish to see Usopp?

00:16:18.370 --> 00:16:20.610
Not this again...

00:16:20.610 --> 00:16:23.270
May I?
I want to talk to him.

00:16:24.610 --> 00:16:25.980
That will not do.

00:16:25.980 --> 00:16:29.220
That man is the village's
biggest exaggerator!

00:16:29.220 --> 00:16:31.050
For someone in your weakened state,

00:16:31.050 --> 00:16:34.190
Usopp's exaggerations
would be too much to handle!

00:16:34.190 --> 00:16:35.290
But...

00:16:35.290 --> 00:16:39.560
Your late parents firmly
instructed me to protect you...

00:16:39.560 --> 00:16:43.630
...to the fullest
of my abilities, Miss Kaya.

00:16:43.630 --> 00:16:46.130
Now then, I'll leave
your medicine here.

00:16:46.130 --> 00:16:48.120
Please be sure to take it.

00:16:52.440 --> 00:16:54.010
Cheapskate.

00:16:54.010 --> 00:16:55.940
"Cheapskate" will do just fine.

00:16:55.940 --> 00:16:57.770
What's bad is bad.

00:17:16.060 --> 00:17:17.720
Pardon the intrusion-

00:17:23.240 --> 00:17:24.840
<i>Usopp-san!</i>

00:17:24.840 --> 00:17:28.140
Heya! You seem as down as ever!

00:17:28.140 --> 00:17:29.480
I'm sorry!

00:17:29.480 --> 00:17:33.610
I'd really like to invite you
in as a real guest...

00:17:33.610 --> 00:17:37.150
...but Klahadore refuses
to allow it...

00:17:37.150 --> 00:17:39.050
He's not a bad person, though.

00:17:39.050 --> 00:17:40.390
Don't sweat it!

00:17:40.390 --> 00:17:43.920
<i>After all,
I am a brave warrior of the sea!</i>

00:17:43.920 --> 00:17:48.500
I'd only feel cramped
inside a house!

00:17:48.500 --> 00:17:51.500
So what adventure are you going
to tell me today?

00:17:51.500 --> 00:17:54.270
Hmm, let's see...

00:17:54.270 --> 00:17:55.500
Alright!

00:17:55.500 --> 00:17:58.510
The story of when I fought the giant
goldfish at the South Pole...

00:17:58.510 --> 00:18:00.010
...when I was five!

00:18:00.010 --> 00:18:01.370
Goldfish?

00:18:01.370 --> 00:18:04.440
Yeah! What first
shocked me...

00:18:04.440 --> 00:18:06.210
...was the immense size
of its poop!

00:18:06.210 --> 00:18:07.880
It was so big that
I landed on it,

00:18:07.880 --> 00:18:10.540
thinking it was
solid ground!

00:18:25.730 --> 00:18:27.270
Is this really the place?!

00:18:27.270 --> 00:18:29.640
Yeah, the pirates
dragged him inside!

00:18:29.640 --> 00:18:30.900
We gotta save him!

00:18:30.900 --> 00:18:32.310
<i>But they're real pirates!</i>

00:18:32.310 --> 00:18:34.070
They might've grilled
and eaten him!

00:18:34.070 --> 00:18:36.940
You idiot!
It's old hags who eat people!

00:18:41.480 --> 00:18:43.970
Alright!
Get ready, you guys!

00:18:45.650 --> 00:18:50.860
This will be the most epic battle
since the Usopp Pirates' formation!

00:18:50.860 --> 00:18:53.330
Yeah!

00:18:53.330 --> 00:18:55.800
The Usopp Pirates have arrived!

00:18:58.670 --> 00:19:00.160
What're they?

00:19:02.300 --> 00:19:05.810
--The captain is gone!
--You don't think he-

00:19:05.810 --> 00:19:07.310
H-hey, pirates!

00:19:07.310 --> 00:19:09.910
What'd you do with
our Captain Usopp?!

00:19:09.910 --> 00:19:12.350
--What'd you do with him?!
--What'd you do with him?!

00:19:12.350 --> 00:19:14.950
That meat was yummy!

00:19:14.950 --> 00:19:17.850
--Meat?!
--Don't tell me the captain-

00:19:19.690 --> 00:19:22.490
W-what?! What did you do?!

00:19:22.490 --> 00:19:24.890
If you're lookin'
for your captain...

00:19:26.560 --> 00:19:27.890
...we ate him.

00:19:31.160 --> 00:19:32.330
Old hag!

00:19:32.330 --> 00:19:34.490
What're you looking
at me for?!

00:19:36.740 --> 00:19:39.070
<i>You just had to say
something stupid!</i>

00:19:42.410 --> 00:19:45.400
Whew, it was just a joke?

00:19:51.150 --> 00:19:53.220
Huge!

00:19:53.220 --> 00:19:56.490
If our captain ran off at this hour,
he'd be here.

00:19:56.490 --> 00:19:59.430
Oh? What's he come here for?

00:19:59.430 --> 00:20:00.990
To lie!

00:20:00.990 --> 00:20:02.530
That's a bad thing!

00:20:02.530 --> 00:20:05.300
He's not bad!
He's great! Right?!

00:20:05.300 --> 00:20:07.170
Yeah! He's great!

00:20:07.170 --> 00:20:09.900
How does that work?

00:20:09.900 --> 00:20:10.870
--Kaya, the girl who lives here,
is weak, and she's had depression...

00:20:10.870 --> 00:20:13.570
--There was a ship
stopped near the goldfish,
--Kaya, the girl who lives here,
is weak, and she's had depression...

00:20:13.570 --> 00:20:14.170
--There was a ship
stopped near the goldfish,
--...ever since her parents died
from an illness a year ago.

00:20:14.170 --> 00:20:17.380
--and on it was a pirate
bigger than even a mountain!
--...ever since her parents died
from an illness a year ago.

00:20:17.380 --> 00:20:18.980
--His face was hilarious!
--...ever since her parents died
from an illness a year ago.

00:20:18.980 --> 00:20:19.650
--His face was hilarious!
--Even though she has lots
of money, she's so sad.

00:20:19.650 --> 00:20:23.050
--Even though she has lots
of money, she's so sad.

00:20:24.250 --> 00:20:28.590
So our captain tells his special
made-up stories to make her laugh!

00:20:28.590 --> 00:20:31.420
'Cause our captain's
the best at telling lies!

00:20:31.420 --> 00:20:34.990
Never heard of a pirate with
a face like that, have you?

00:20:34.990 --> 00:20:37.200
Oh, so he's great!

00:20:37.200 --> 00:20:38.200
Yeah!

00:20:38.200 --> 00:20:41.940
I like the captain's
meddling side!

00:20:41.940 --> 00:20:44.370
I like his bossy side!

00:20:44.370 --> 00:20:46.840
I like his exaggerating side!

00:20:46.840 --> 00:20:49.840
So that's helped her feel
a little better?

00:20:49.840 --> 00:20:51.810
Yeah, a lot better!

00:20:51.810 --> 00:20:55.720
Great! Let's ask her for
a ship after all!

00:20:55.720 --> 00:20:59.050
<i>It's thanks to Usopp
that she's gotten better.</i>

00:20:59.050 --> 00:21:01.150
Just getting in is impossible!

00:21:01.150 --> 00:21:03.990
<i>There are way strong guards
at the gate!</i>

00:21:03.990 --> 00:21:05.630
--Huh?
--Where'd Luffy go?

00:21:05.630 --> 00:21:07.890
I'll go ask!

00:21:07.890 --> 00:21:09.200
Wait, you're not gonna-?!

00:21:09.200 --> 00:21:11.690
Gum-Gum...

00:21:13.700 --> 00:21:16.140
--H-his arms stretched!
--He's a monster!

00:21:16.140 --> 00:21:17.240
...Pardon...

00:21:17.240 --> 00:21:19.770
--Hey!
--Wait, Luffy!

00:21:19.770 --> 00:21:23.140
...the Intrusion!

00:21:24.580 --> 00:21:31.250
...And so we escaped into the sky
atop a gigantic slingshot ball!

00:21:32.450 --> 00:21:33.780
Huh?

00:21:34.790 --> 00:21:36.780
Yahoo!

00:21:44.760 --> 00:21:47.570
--That worked great!
--Did not!

00:21:47.570 --> 00:21:50.000
A-are you all right?!

00:21:50.000 --> 00:21:52.310
Yeah! It's okay, it's okay!

00:21:52.310 --> 00:21:55.480
They're new recruits who heard
all about me and came from afar...

00:21:55.480 --> 00:21:58.440
...to join the Usopp Pirates!

00:21:58.440 --> 00:22:01.310
No, not me!

00:22:01.310 --> 00:22:03.320
I'm here to ask a favor!

00:22:03.320 --> 00:22:04.820
A favor? Of me?

00:22:04.820 --> 00:22:07.520
Yeah! We want a big ship-

00:22:07.520 --> 00:22:10.320
You, there!

00:22:10.320 --> 00:22:13.120
What are you doing?!

00:22:14.230 --> 00:22:15.890
Klahadore...

00:22:17.330 --> 00:22:22.740
I don't appreciate you breaking
in here without permission!

00:22:27.110 --> 00:22:28.970
Who's he?

00:22:56.070 --> 00:23:06.070
<i>When I was little, I had
a vision of a treasure map</i>

00:23:10.280 --> 00:23:17.220
<i>and I always searched
for that miraculous place</i>

00:23:17.220 --> 00:23:24.390
<i>before someone else could
beat me to it</i>

00:23:26.930 --> 00:23:36.930
<i>If the world is going to change</i>

00:23:38.410 --> 00:23:45.420
<i>before I can even attain my dream</i>

00:23:45.420 --> 00:23:52.490
<i>then take me to the time
when I knew nothing</i>

00:23:52.490 --> 00:24:02.490
<i>so that my memories won't fade</i>
